share-dialog-views-with-settings-consumers

Lane: cross

Unit: host-dialogs-with-shared-resources

ChildPatch: share-dialog-views-with-settings-consumers

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Adapt native settings dialogs to the centered Control Center host without a composer anchor.

Requires: none

Provides: Native text, masked-input and selection views with current editing preferences and list controls; a Control Center dialog stack owns nested completion, covered selection refresh, input and redraw scheduling over the supplied backdrop.

Boundary: Keep the ordinary BottomPane host, Escape interruption confirmation and permission shortcuts on their native input-area path. Feature consumers retain settings content, RPCs and failures. Preserve native widgets, exact input and cancellation without routing Control Center state through ChatWidget.

Verification: Focused masking, configured list controls, nested accept and cancel, covered selection refresh, input isolation, frame scheduling and centered rendering tests, followed by Proxy, Telegram and Control Center integration tests.

CrossGroup: control-center


